<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-7339] RENTING partition is not evicted after restore from storage</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-7339</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;If partition was in RENTING state at the moment when node is stopped, then after restart it is not evicted.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It seems it is an issue in GridDhtLocalPartition.rent, &apos;tryEvictAsync&apos; is not called is partition was already in RENTING state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Also there is error in GridDhtPartitionTopologyImpl.checkEvictions: partition state is always treated as changed after part.rent call even if part.rent does not actually change state.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
