                            <comment id="16505935" author="jokser" created="Fri, 8 Jun 2018 11:46:22 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=ascherbakov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;ascherbakov&quot;&gt;ascherbakov&lt;/a&gt; I&apos;ve looked at changes and have 2 proposals to improve the solution:&lt;br/&gt;
1) To prevent partition eviction/renting you can explicitly reserve it using group reservation (org.apache.ignite.internal.processors.cache.distributed.dht.GridDhtLocalPartition#addReservation), so there is no needs to introduce new debug/test variables.&lt;br/&gt;
2) The logic of invoking &quot;clearAsync&quot; during restore process can be moved to org.apache.ignite.internal.processors.cache.distributed.dht.GridDhtPartitionTopology#afterStateRestored callback, to avoid GridCacheDatabaseSharedManager restore logic overload.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
